============================================================
PIPELINE LB6 EXPERIMENT (register-pressure recovery via launch_bounds)
============================================================
Date:           2026-08-13
Platform:       win32, sm_120 (RTX 5060), CUDA 13.3
Variant source: kernels/src/register_tiled_gemm_TMA_B_pipeline_lb6.cu
                (byte-for-byte copy of the working pipelined source; the ONLY
                 change is adding __launch_bounds__(256, 6) to the kernel)
Accepted source: kernels/src/register_tiled_gemm.cu (UNCHANGED)

VERDICT: REJECT
  __launch_bounds__(256,6) successfully restored the 6-block / ~80% occupancy
  resource bracket with zero spills, BUT it did NOT improve wall-clock: the lb6
  candidate is consistently SLOWER than the unconstrained 47-register pipeline
  (+0.4% run1, +2.7% run2). Occupancy was not the binding cost; the extra
  registers in the original encode more ILP per iteration and win wall-clock.

